<%# Idle renders nothing — an empty queue is self-evident from the empty card
    right below, and "Nothing importing right now." was a line of text saying so
    a second time.

    The wrapper stays in the DOM regardless, exactly as _footer_note does, because
    index.turbo_stream.erb targets #queue-status-text with turbo_stream.replace:
    drop the element and the poll has nothing to patch, so an import that starts
    while this screen is already open (the share extension, with the app
    backgrounded) would never get its "N imports in progress" line. `contents`
    keeps the empty wrapper from occupying a line box. %>
<div id="queue-status-text" class="contents">
  <% if active_count.positive? %>
    <p class="text-app-text-2 text-sm mt-1">
      <%= pluralize(active_count, "import") %> in progress — we'll ping you when they're ready.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
